rd leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Saffron City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Sabrina, HM Fly — a girl in the hidden house on Route 16, just west of Celadon behind a cuttable tree, teaches your team to fly you between towns — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Sabrina is step two, not a competing choice. Word on the road about Sabrina: people whisper about her — PSYCHIC-types, sees your moves coming; ghosts and bugs are the folk remedy YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): Five badges in — Brock, Misty, Surge, Erika, Koga. Surf should be opening the seas. Next is Sabrina in Saffron (Marsh Badge).. Next on my list: catch an diglett around Diglett\'s Cave. It grows into my dugtrio — that\'s my answer for Blaine AND Agatha down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA."; "Now that you have the SOULBADGE, the DEFENSE of your POK.MON rises. It also lets you SURF outside of battle. Ah! Take this, too!". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Saffron City for the Marsh Badge. Next: You beat Koga — ride the momentum: Sabrina in Saffron City is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Saffron City, beat Sabrina for the Marsh Badge. Your team right now: blastoise (L54), ekans (L16), spearow (L18), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat 