   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in Saffron City — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center and a Mart; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 8; Route 10; Route 12. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. Field moves ready: CUT.. Okay — to get past this I need HM Fly — a girl in the hidden house on Route 16, just west of Celadon behind a cuttable tree, teaches your team to fly you between towns. Heads up: you have ZERO Poké Balls — you literally can\'t catch a teammate until you buy some at a Mart, so a Mart run has to come before any catching.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 6 of 8 — next is Sabrina in Saffron City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Saffron City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Sabrina, HM Fly — a girl in the hidden house on Route 16, just west of Celadon behind a cuttable tree, teaches your team to fly you between towns — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Sabrina is step two, not a competing choice. Word on the road about Sabrina: people whisper about her — PSYCHIC-types, sees your moves coming; ghosts and bugs are the folk remedy YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): Five badges in — Brock, Misty, Surge, Erika, Koga. Surf should be opening the seas. Next is Sabrina in Saffron (Marsh Badge).. Next on my list: catch an diglett around Diglett\'s Cave. It grows into my dugtrio — that\'s my answer for Blaine AND Agatha down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA."; "Now that you have the SOULBADGE, the DEFENSE of your POK.MON rises. It also lets you SURF outside of battle. Ah! Take this, too!". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Saffron City for the Marsh Badge. Next: You beat Koga — ride the momentum: Sabrina in Saffron City is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Saffron City, beat Sabrina for the Marsh Badge. Your team right now: blastoise (L54), ekans (L16), spearow (L18), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "5 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul). Next gym: Sabrina of Saffron City. Pokédex: 12 caught. She's five badges, well past halfway — the Elite Four's coming into view (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'blastoise (L54), ekans (L16), spearow (L18), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and head to Saffron City for the Marsh Badge", 'medium': 'You beat Koga — ride the momentum: Sabrina in Saffron City is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training', 'long': 'Reach Saffron City, beat Sabrina for the Marsh Badge'}, 'strategy': '1) WAR PREP: next is Sabrina (psychic, ~L38-43). Your answer on the team: butterfree — lead with it and keep it healthy.\n2) TEAM BUILD: diglett -> dugtrio answers Blaine, Agatha, Champion.\n3) DEX PUSH: 12/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n4) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace.'} options=['swap_keeper']

